# Save a one-shot, backend-agnostic global point-cloud map suitable for
# loading directly into a path planner (e.g. FAR planner via /scan_cloud).
#
# Source: the accumulated /registered_scan cloud in the map frame.
# Works with both ARISE (arise_slam_mid360) and lightning-lm, since both
# publish /registered_scan with their global-frame transform applied.

# Output file path (without extension). If empty, the launch-time
# exploredAreaFile path is used with a timestamp suffix.
string file_path

# Voxel leaf size, in meters, applied to the snapshot before writing.
# 0 = use the launch-time mapVoxelSize default (0.1 m, matches FAR
# indoor.yaml voxel_dim). Increase for sparser, planner-only maps;
# decrease for denser maps for visualization.
float64 voxel_size

# Also save the FAR planner visibility graph as <file_path>.vgh, by
# publishing the path on /save_file_dir. FAR planner's graph_decoder
# writes one text file containing every node's position, free_direct,
# surface dirs, is_covered/is_frontier/is_navpoint/is_boundary flags and
# four neighbor lists (connect/poly/contour/trajectory). The freespace
# vgraph is the poly-connect subset between is_covered nodes, so it is
# already captured by this single save. Has no effect if graph_decoder
# is not running (e.g. FAR planner not launched).
bool save_vgraph true
---
bool success
string message
uint32 num_points
# Path of the .vgh sibling that was requested on /save_file_dir. Empty
# when save_vgraph is false, no path is derivable, or graph_decoder is
# not subscribed. Note: the actual write is performed by graph_decoder
# asynchronously, so a non-empty value here means the request was
# published, not that the file exists.
string vgraph_path
